  "result": "I wrote the test and checked it both ways: it passes on the before snapshot and fails on the after snapshot. The failure is on the card's background color, not an import error or a crash.\n\nIt finds the Savings Accounts card by the flagged selector (`section:nth-child(3) > div:nth-child(2)`) at the top level of the page. It then checks that the card's `background-color` is `rgb(220, 252, 231)`, the value from the before snapshot. On the after snapshot it fails with `expected rgb(220, 252, 231), got rgb(254, 202, 202)`, caused by the change from `background:#dcfce7` to `#fecaca` in `section#cards`.\n\nThe test is in `test_generated_regression.py` in this folder.",
